eturn on equity."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 1.9% over 3 years, 3.9% over 5 years and 4.3% over 10 years.","At current returns, reinvesting 7% of profits supports about 0.8% a year of fundamental growth, too little to drive meaningful growth.","It has missed earnings estimates by 14.5% on average.","Analysts expect 19.7% long-term annual earnings growth."],"own":["Insiders own 5.7%, meaningful skin in the game, and institutions hold 18%.","Insiders have only bought over the past year (9 purchases).","It returns 3.3% a year to shareholders (1.0% in buybacks and 2.8% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 0.9% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","It has paid a dividend for 17 consecutive years, though it has been cut 1.1% a year over the last five."],"people":["With about 341 employees, each generates about $230K of revenue, 0.5x the Financial Services median, and productivity has risen 3.3% a year.","That works out to $68K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $653K (3x revenue per employee).","Stock compensation averages $1K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"WATCH","conv":64,"head":"Watch: no strong case either way.","pros":["Trades 49% below fair value of $79.92","Insiders net buyers ($6K over 12 months)","Returns 3.3% a year to shareholders"],"cons":[],"flags":[],"need":["the model rates it HOLD"],"buy_below":67.93,"vc":{"base":79.92,"base_src":"dcf","bear":55.91,"bull":120.92,"alt_median":35.84,"n_alt":3,"gap":1.2296,"dispersion":0.0846,"level":"LOW","why":["DCF is 123% above the other models' median ($35.84)"]},"med":{"pe":12.155,"ev_ebitda":10.862,"pfcf":12.9041,"pb":1.3934,"roic":0.116,"gross_margin":0.4181,"fcf_margin":0.2507,"div_yield":0.0265}},"ticker":"ISBA","date":"2026-11-06"}